\pard\widctlpar\sa160\sl252\slmult1 There are a couple of options to discuss:\par
\ul\b Search and Replace Options / left Panel\par

\pard{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf3\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\fi-360\li720\sa160\sl252\slmult1\ulnone\b0 Directory tree\line includes all local filesystems (Disk, CD, mapped Network Drives)\line Expand and select an appropriate directory for your search\line Searching big numbers and large files requires more time to complete.\par

\pard{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf3\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\fi-360\li1080\sa160\sl252\slmult1 Include subdirectories\line controls if only the selected directory or all subdirectories are included in the search run \par

\pard\li360\sa160\sl252\slmult1 ==> Drag and drop network directories from Windows Explorer into the Directory Tree panel to add them temporarily for a FindReplace run.\par

\pard{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf3\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\fi-360\li720\sa160\sl252\slmult1 Filenames\line the utility processes only text-files like .txt, .log, .cmd, .cs, .sql. \line It is not able to read Word (.doc), Excel and PDF files. An internal routine excludes more than 60 known file extensions like .zip, .mp3, .mov, .jpg, .xls, .cab and others. The number of skipped files is reported in the status message after a Find/Replace run.\line\line multiple mime types, delimited with \ldblquote ,\rdblquote  or \ldblquote ;\rdblquote  may be specified\line -> Example: \tab Filenames: *.cmd;*.bat;*.sql; *.ini;*.config;*.log\line -> Default:\tab Filenames: *\par

\pard{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf3\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\fi-360\li1080\sa160\sl252\slmult1 Select by date\line is an additional criteria to limit the number of files. If you have lots of Job logfiles, but you are only interested in files from the last some days, then use this option.\par

\pard{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf3\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\fi-360\li720\sa160\sl252\slmult1 Find Text\line Your text or expression to search\par

\pard{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf3\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\fi-360\li1080\sa160\sl252\slmult1 Match Case\tab                             \line controls case sensivity. Default: ignore case\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}Match Word\tab\tab\line search-string on a word boundary\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}Regular Expression\tab\tab\line search-string is a regular expression\par

\pard{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf3\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\fi-360\li720\sa160\sl252\slmult1 Replace Text\line Is the string which will replace the "Find Text".\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}Button FIND\line creates a list of selected files and then examines each file. \par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}Button REPLACE\line uses the find routine to get the list of files with matches, archives the file (if option \i Backup \i0 is selected) and replaces the found string.\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}Button CANCEL\line Once FIND or REPLACE is running, button CANCEL is available. It stops the running process and returns \par

\pard\widctlpar\sa160\sl252\slmult1\ul\b Tab: Result\par
\ulnone\b0 The Directory/File List is the result of a previous Find process. Only Files where the search string was found are displayed. By selecting a file, its content is displayed in a Textbox in the right panel.\par
Right Mouse click opens a context-menu where several file options are available:\par

\pard{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf3\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\fi-360\li720\sa160\sl252\slmult1 Explorer\tab\line starts the Windows Explorer of the selected directory.\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}Open\tab\tab\line starts the default application for that file-type.\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}Replace\tab               \line replaced \i Find Text \i0 with \i Replace Text \i0 in the selected file.\line If a backup option is active, then the original file is archived.\line File Preview is automatically refreshed after a Replace.\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}Restore\tab               \line when something went wrong - and a backup option was selected - you may restore to a earlier version.\line File Preview is automatically refreshed after a Restore.\par

\pard\widctlpar\sa160\sl252\slmult1\ul\b Tab: Result, Split-Screen File Preview\par
\ulnone\b0 By clicking on a file in the middle panel, its contents is displayed in a Read-Only RichTextBox. The Find-String is marked; automatically scrolled to its first occurrence. \par
You might test \ldblquote Find Text\rdblquote  variants within this file; verify more complex regular expressions, before running a search in a directory tree.\par
\ul\b Tab: Options \par

\pard{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf3\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\fi-360\li720\sa160\sl252\slmult1\ulnone\b0 Backup and Restore\ul\b\line\ulnone\b0 Backup definitions are processed when the tool replaces the content of a file.\line Backups are file archives in a .zip file. Multiple versions for the same file could exist - the tool itself garantees, that only one version of a certain modification date is stored. If multiple version exist, then the user select the appropriate version from a list in the Restore operation.\line There is the option to store the backup \f1 file (FindReplace_Backup.zip\lang2055 ) in the directory where the updated file is located or as a central backup file in a common directory.\line Optionally, you might completly skip the backup part. Maybe you've got already a valid backup of the related files ?\ul\b\f0\lang1033\line\line\ulnone\b0\f1\lang2055 Use the \b Restore \b0 option in the tab \b Result,  \b0 to go back to an older version of a file. Outside FindReplace, use \b 7zip\b0  to view/restore the contents of FindReplace_Backup.zip\ul\b\f0\lang1033\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}\ulnone\b0\f1\lang2055 Drag and Drop\ul\b\f0\lang1033\line\ulnone\b0\f1\lang2055 When you drag and drop a directory from Windows Explorer (e.g.  {\f2{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "\\\\\\\\REMOTEPC\\\\c$"}}{\fldrslt{\\\\REMOTEPC\\c$\ul0\cf0}}}}\f1\fs22   ) to the FindReplace, then it has to map the network directory to a drive letter first. At application close, it is automatically unmapped.\ul\b\f0\lang1033\line\ulnone\b0\f1\lang2055 Default is letter \b A \b0 - define your preferred letter here.\ul\b\f0\lang1033\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}\ulnone\b0\f1\lang2055 Personalize\ul\b\f0\lang1033\line\ulnone\b0\f1\lang2055 Choose your Theme and Color Scheme\ul\b\f0\lang1033\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}\ulnone\b0\f1\lang2055 Update Check\ul\b\f0\lang1033\line\ulnone\b0\f1\lang2055 Checks for a new version on my GitHub repository. You'll be prompted, if a newer version is available. The updater replaces the current version and restarts the program.\ul\b\f0\lang1033\line\ulnone\b0\f1\lang2055 An internet connection is required for that process.\ul\b\f0\lang1033\par

\pard\sa160\sl252\slmult1 Tab: Favorites\par

\pard{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf3\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\fi-360\li720\sa160\sl252\slmult1\ulnone\b0 Historical searches\ul\b\line\ulnone\b0 Here you save and manage your epic search definitions and add a short description to it.\ul\b\line\ulnone\b0 With the use of a context menu option (Mouse right click), you load or execute a saved search.\ul\b\line\ulnone\b0 Double Click does the load and find trick in one go.\ul\b\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}\ulnone\b0 Button ADD saves your current selections/options into this list - and finally into file Favorites.xml \ul\b\par

\pard\widctlpar\sa160\sl252\slmult1\par
Find in more details\par
\ulnone\b0 FindReplace is written in C# and uses Regex.Matches as a find command.\line Escape character is \\\par
\ul Examples\par

\pard{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf3\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\fi-360\li720\sa160\sl252\slmult1\ulnone Find: \tab\tab\tab "Database", "database" or "DATABASE"\line Find Text: \tab\tab database\line Match Word:\tab\tab checked\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}Find\tab\tab\tab 2018/05 or 2018/06 or 2018/07 or 2018/08 or 2018/09\line Find Text\tab\tab 2018/0[5-9]\line Regular Expression:\tab checked\line Explanation:\tab\tab use a regular expression to find a range of values [5-9]\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}Find\tab\tab\tab "Canon" or "Nikon"\line Find Text: \tab\tab (Canon|Nikon)\line Match Case:\tab\tab checked\line Match Word\tab\tab checked\line Regular Expression\tab checked\line Explanation\tab\tab use a regular expression with the alternate construct ( | ) to match any one element seperated by the vertical bar\par

\pard{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf3\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\widctlpar\fi-360\li720\sa160\sl252\slmult1 Find\tab\tab\tab Oracle Error-Message (ORA-00600, TNS-12345), but exclude RMAN-08137 in *.log files from the last 2 weeks\line File Names\tab\tab *.log\line Select by Date\tab\tab checked\line Max Days\tab\tab 14\line Find Text\tab\tab (\\b(?!RMAN-08137)[A-Z]\{3,5\}-\\d\{3,5\})\line Match Case:\tab\tab checked\line Regular Expression\tab checked\line Explanation:\tab\tab use negative lookahead (?!RMAN-08137) to exclude that string from search\par

\pard\widctlpar\li720\sa160\sl252\slmult1\par

